      <h2>Driving License Rules for Expats</h2>
      <p>Spain recognizes foreign driving licenses under certain conditions. However, the rules depend on how long you're staying and your home country.</p>

      <h3>First 6 Months: Your Home Country License Works</h3>
      <p>As a tourist or new resident, you can drive with your valid license from home for up to 6 months. You must carry:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your original license (not a copy)</li>
        <li>Passport</li>
        <li>International Driving Permit (IDP) recommended for renters and authorities</li>
        <li>Proof of car insurance</li>
        <li>Vehicle registration documents</li>
      </ul>

      <p><strong>After 6 months of residency:</strong> You must exchange your license for a Spanish one (Permiso de Conducción) or you cannot legally drive.</p>

      <h3>License Exchange by Country</h3>

      <h4>UK Drivers</h4>
      <p>UK holds a reciprocal agreement with Spain. Your UK license exchanges for Spanish without a written test (though a practical driving test may be required in some cases). Contact DGT (Dirección General de Tráfico) or apply at a traffic office.</p>

      <h4>US Drivers (All States)</h4>
      <p>The US does not have a license reciprocity agreement. Most states' licenses do not directly exchange. You'll likely need to pass a Spanish driving test and written exam (in Spanish). Study materials available online.</p>

      <h4>Canadian Drivers</h4>
      <p>Canada has no reciprocal agreement. Your license converts but you may need a practical driving test. Check with your provincial motor vehicle authority before moving.</p>

      <h4>Australian Drivers</h4>
      <p>Australia has limited reciprocity. You can drive on Australian license initially, but exchange after 6 months. Practical test may be required.</p>

      <h3>International Driving Permit (IDP)</h3>
      <p>An IDP is an official translation of your license. It's not a replacement, but an add-on. Recommended for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Car rentals (some companies require it)</li>
        <li>Travel outside your home country within first 6 months</li>
        <li>Proof of license validity to Spanish authorities</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Get an IDP from your home country's automobile authority (DVLA in UK, DMV in US, etc.) before traveling. Cost: €5-15. Valid for 3 years.</p>

      <div class="msv__cta-mid">
        <h3>Need Help Navigating Spanish Residency?</h3>
        <p>License exchanges, padrón registration, and other bureaucratic processes are easier with professional support. Many gestorías handle driving license applications.</p>
